<exercisegroup xml:id="exercisegroup-orthog-angle-size-Rn">
<title>Size of angle in <m> \R^n </m></title>

<introduction><p>
	In each case:
	<ol>
		<li> Use the dot product to determine if the angle between <m> \uvec{v} </m> and <m> \uvec{w} </m> is acute, right, or obtuse. </li>
		<li> Are <m> \uvec{v} </m> and <m> \uvec{w} </m> <term><xref ref="definition-orthog-orthogonal" text="custom">orthogonal</xref></term>? </li>
	</ol>
</p></introduction>

<exercise>

	<statement><p>
		<m> \uvec{v} = (-1,3,0) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{w} = (-5,2,4) </m>
	</p></statement>

	<answer><p><ol>

		<li> Acute: <m> \udotprod{v}{w} = 11 \gt 0 </m>. </li>

		<li> No. </li>

	</ol></p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p>
		<m> \uvec{v} = (1,3,6) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{w} = (6,1,-2) </m>
	</p></statement>

	<answer><p><ol>

		<li> Obtuse: <m> \udotprod{v}{w} = -3 \lt 0 </m>. </li>

		<li> No. </li>

	</ol></p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p>
		<m> \uvec{v} = (3,6,1,2) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{w} = (1,0,-1,-1) </m>
	</p></statement>

	<answer><p><ol>

		<li> Right: <m> \udotprod{v}{w} = 0 </m>. </li>

		<li> Yes. </li>

	</ol></p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p>
		<m> \uvec{v} = (-3,-3, 4,-4, 2) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{w} = ( 1,-1,-2,-2,-4) </m>
	</p></statement>

	<answer><p><ol>

		<li> Obtuse: <m> \udotprod{v}{w} = -8 \lt 0 </m>. </li>

		<li> No. </li>

	</ol></p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p>
		<m> \uvec{v} = (-3,-3, 4,-4, 2) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{w} = ( 1,-1,-2,-2, 0) </m>
	</p></statement>

	<answer><p><ol>

		<li> Right: <m> \udotprod{v}{w} = 0 </m>. </li>

		<li> Yes. </li>

	</ol></p></answer>

</exercise>

</exercisegroup>
